        a_en: "For a database, either point the test suite at a real but disposable test database — resetting its state between test runs — or use an in-memory alternative like mongodb-memory-server for quick, isolated unit tests. For external API calls, jest.mock() replaces the whole module with a controlled fake implementation, or a library like nock intercepts outgoing HTTP requests at the network level and returns a predetermined canned response, so tests stay fast and don't depend on a real third-party service actually being reachable during a test run.",
        a_hi: "Database ke liye, ya to test suite ko ek real lekin disposable test database pe point karo (test runs ke beech uski state reset karke), ya mongodb-memory-server jaisa in-memory alternative use karo quick, isolated unit tests ke liye. External API calls ke liye, jest.mock() poore module ko ek controlled fake implementation se replace kar deta hai, ya nock jaisi library network level pe outgoing HTTP requests intercept karke ek predetermined canned response de deti hai — isse tests fast rehte hain aur test run ke dauraan kisi real third-party service ke actually reachable hone pe depend nahi karte.",
