        q: "What is graceful shutdown and how do you implement it in Node.js?",
        a_en: "Graceful shutdown means finishing in-flight requests and cleanly closing open resources — database connections, message queue connections — before the process actually exits, instead of dying mid-request and dropping active work on the floor. It's implemented by listening for process.on('SIGTERM', ...), the signal a platform like Kubernetes or a process manager sends before terminating a process, calling server.close() to stop accepting brand-new connections while letting in-flight ones finish naturally, then closing the database pool and other resources, and finally calling process.exit() once everything has actually wound down cleanly.",
        a_hi: "Graceful shutdown ka matlab hai in-flight requests ko poora karna aur open resources (database connections, message queue connections) ko cleanly band karna process ke actually exit hone se pehle, request ke beech me hi mar kar active work ko drop karne ki jagah. Yeh process.on('SIGTERM', ...) sun kar implement hota hai — yeh signal Kubernetes jaisa platform ya ek process manager process terminate karne se pehle bhejta hai — phir server.close() call karke bilkul nayi connections accept karna band karo (jabki in-flight wali naturally poori hone do), phir database pool aur baaki resources band karo, aur finally jab sab kuch actually cleanly wind down ho jaaye tab process.exit() call karo.",
