        q: "How do you debug an issue that only happens in production, not locally?",
        a_en: "Start with structured logs and APM traces — Datadog, New Relic — since reproducing the bug locally often isn't possible in the first place if it's environment- or scale-dependent. Check for environment-specific differences: different environment variable values, a different database size that changes query performance characteristics, or load and concurrency that only shows up under real production traffic. If genuinely necessary, remote-debug carefully with node --inspect on a staging environment that mirrors production, and add temporary, well-scoped extra logging around the suspected code path to narrow down the exact failure point before removing it again.",
        a_hi: "Structured logs aur APM traces (Datadog, New Relic) se shuru karo, kyunki agar bug environment- ya scale-dependent hai to use locally reproduce karna shuru se hi possible nahi hota. Environment-specific differences check karo: alag environment variable values, alag database size jo query performance characteristics badal deta hai, ya load/concurrency jo sirf real production traffic ke neeche dikhta hai. Agar genuinely zaroori ho, to production jaisa staging environment pe carefully node --inspect se remote-debug karo, aur suspected code path ke around temporary, well-scoped extra logging add karo exact failure point narrow down karne ke liye, phir use wapas hata do.",
