        q: "What is a webhook and how would you implement one securely?",
        a_en: "A webhook is a server-to-server callback — instead of your app polling a third-party service repeatedly asking 'anything new yet?', that service calls a URL on your app the instant a relevant event happens, such as Stripe notifying your backend the moment a payment actually succeeds. To implement one securely, verify the request's signature, sent in a header and computed using a shared secret, to confirm the payload genuinely came from the claimed sender and wasn't forged; respond quickly, typically within seconds, since most providers expect a fast acknowledgment and will otherwise retry aggressively; and handle actual processing asynchronously after that quick acknowledgment rather than making the sender wait on it.",
        a_hi: "Webhook ek server-to-server callback hai — apni app se baar-baar third-party service ko poll karke 'kuch naya hai kya?' poochne ki jagah, woh service ek relevant event hote hi apni app ke ek URL ko call kar deti hai, jaise Stripe payment actually succeed hote hi turant apne backend ko notify kar deta hai. Ise securely implement karne ke liye: request ka signature verify karo (jo ek header me bhejaa jaata hai aur ek shared secret se compute hota hai) yeh confirm karne ke liye ki payload genuinely claimed sender se aaya hai, forge nahi hua; jaldi respond karo (typically seconds ke andar), kyunki zyaadatar providers fast acknowledgment expect karte hain aur warna aggressively retry karte hain; aur actual processing ko us quick acknowledgment ke baad asynchronously handle karo, sender ko uska wait karwane ki jagah.",
